ed with the whole  she has to make her way in a man's world  think of a I figure this woman more than  paid her dues you know during World War  Two and I mean I get that you know  society as a whole hadn't gotten to the  point where a woman can you know is  expected to hold up the same as a man  but I mean come on they set her back so  much that's like did anybody look at her  military record but we got you know sort  of this proto version  the Black Widow program and we got some  fun with the Howling Commandos and and  it was nice it was pleasant it was fun  number 14 agent Carter season 2 why am i  right giving a ranking above the other  one well it just feels like they hit  their rhythm a little bit better now  full disclosure I did not actually get  to finish this season for whatever  reason my DVR just got weird and stopped  recording it and I didn't care enough to  finish and you think that would make me  rank it below season one but I don't  know overall it felt more comfortable it  felt it felt less like it was trying to  prove something and there's nothing  wrong with trying to prove something but  I like the more easygoing feel of the  about half a season in ourselves that I  saw worth of agent Carter season 2  number 13 Iron Man 3 now I know there  are some people who cannot stand Iron  Man 3 largely because of the twist  involving the Mandarin I actually think  it was kind of a clever twist but they  didn't execute it as well as they could  have but again it's got a lot of great  moments in it's got a lot of great ideas  in it I like the iron Legion I actually  like Tony with that kid that whole  segment I thought worked really well but  there are lots of little things that are  just if the guide Pierce's killing is  not a particularly great villain the  relationship drama with Pepper Potts I  really could have done with that I  really loved their dynamic and the first  one where you know it's not even a will  they won't Lee it's just like a they're  rea